WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:04.620
So when it comes to staying informed about
the pandemic, we are getting very different

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:07.500
messages from different messengers.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:12.350
And we have a new poll that has very quickly
helped told us that Donald Trump is not one

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:18.489
of the most trusted messengers for the American
people, although his approval rating is actually

00:00:18.489 --> 00:00:19.489
up.

00:00:19.489 --> 00:00:23.169
And I'm going to talk about that seeming incongruity
in a moment.

00:00:23.169 --> 00:00:28.999
It may not surprise you that New York Governor
Andrew Cuomo and Dr. Anthony Foushee, who's

00:00:28.999 --> 00:00:33.100
one of the top infectious disease experts
in the country, who's been a fixture of at

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.309
least some of Trump's press briefings.

00:00:35.309 --> 00:00:39.370
They are the most trusted people for guidance
on the pandemic.

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:44.480
And the poll asked, when it comes to official
advice regarding Corona virus, please rate

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.710
how much you trust the following messengers
on a scale from 1 to 5.

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:50.800
Of course, a higher number being more trusted.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:57.379
Dr. Anthony Foushee at the top at 3.8 for
followed by Andrew Cuomo at 3.2 9.

00:00:57.379 --> 00:01:01.280
Dr. Deborah Burke's close behind at 3.1.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:07.980
Democratic California Governor Gavin Newsome
at 2.9 7, followed by Joe Biden, then Mike

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:09.140
Pence.

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:13.590
And Donald Trump is trusted only more than
Stephen Manoogian.

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:15.520
So it looks to put it a different way.

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:20.820
Only Stephen Manoogian is less trusted when
it comes to coronavirus than Donald Trump.

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:22.860
So I have a few different thoughts on this.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:28.950
So on the one hand, there's no question that,
of course, Foushee and Cuomo are more trustworthy

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:30.510
than Donald Trump.

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:31.619
That's the reality.

00:01:31.619 --> 00:01:34.250
It's good that the polls reflect that.

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:38.990
The other side of it is, though, the numbers
should be far more stark.

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:43.649
I mean, the degree to which Anthony Foushee
and Andrew Cuomo present facts and live in

00:01:43.649 --> 00:01:47.340
the real world compared to the degree with
which Donald Trump is living in a fantasy

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.510
world with just lies and distortions.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.950
You would hope that the numbers were more
than you know.

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:55.040
One point, something points apart.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:58.460
But let me talk about the other side of this
for a second, because Donald Trump's approval

00:01:58.460 --> 00:01:59.930
rating is up.

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:04.420
The portion of the population that believes
Donald Trump is handling Corona virus properly

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:05.420
is quite high.

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:08.720
It's much higher than anyone who's been paying
attention in a real way would expect it to

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:09.720
be.

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.410
And so it seems like there's a disconnect
there.

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:16.300
How can Donald Trump be so not trusted when
it comes to the specifics of coronavirus,

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:20.300
while at the same time he's got the highest
approval rating of his presidency, or at least

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:23.000
tied with the highest approval rating of his
presidency?

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:26.480
I don't think there is as much of a disconnect
there as some people might think.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:28.060
Here's what's going on.

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:35.410
It appears that on the facts, most Americans
realize what Donald Trump says about the virus

00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:36.740
is not accurate.

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:38.890
He's either lying, he's incompetent.

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:41.530
He doesn't know he's being deceptive.

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:47.190
But at the same time that Americans recognize
that, we know that during national crises

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:50.880
there is a degree of a rally around the president
effect.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:55.470
It's only a few points of approval that Donald
Trump has gained, and that's probably what

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:56.670
explains it.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:03:00.740
Trump, because of the rally around the president
mentality during a crisis, in this case, a

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:04.860
pandemic has gained a little bit of approval
there.

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:08.730
But on the facts, Americans realize that the
guy is a buffoon when it comes to coronavirus.

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:12.730
Now, there's another issue that's probably
a factor in the United States.

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:18.940
We've got very densely populated areas and
very rural depopulated areas.

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:23.980
Right now, it's much more the densely populated
areas that are having the corona virus cases

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:25.300
and the deaths.

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:31.720
So there are probably lots of people who are
saying, I'm not seeing many cases in my area.

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:33.530
I don't know of anybody who's got it.

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:35.250
I'm not hearing about death.

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:40.950
So therefore, Donald Trump must be handling
this well while simultaneously realizing when

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:46.620
they hear Trump speak that on the facts of
the day to day, he probably can't be trusted.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:50.600
Now, when it comes to Dr. Foushee, there are
more and more questions about how long he's

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:56.050
going to be allowed to have a public presence
because he doesn't seem completely onboard

00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:58.800
with every idiotic thing that Donald Trump
says.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:03.270
Although there's some limit to how much he
can express that that disagreement publicly,

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:08.330
there is no doubt that despite Donald Trump
saying two days ago when he was asked, is

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:12.550
everything okay with you and Dr. Foushee,
he said, of course, of course, of course.

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:19.930
My if I found out in a few days that Foushee
was gone or resigned, it would not be a huge

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:20.930
surprise.

00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:23.770
I'm not saying I expect it to happen, but
it would not be surprising.

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:27.729
Could be a combination of, you know, Trump
gets very jealous.

00:04:27.729 --> 00:04:32.210
People seem to like and trust Dr. Foushee
much more as we see from this poll.

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:33.699
Trump's not going to like that.

00:04:33.699 --> 00:04:38.879
Additionally, Dr. Foushee, I can't imagine,
is going to say let's let her rip on April

00:04:38.879 --> 00:04:39.879
12.

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:41.330
That could create a point of conflict.

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:45.639
It wouldn't be shocking to me if we never
see Dr. Foushee again, at least with Donald

00:04:45.639 --> 00:04:46.639
Trump.

00:04:46.639 --> 00:04:47.639
After a few days.

00:04:47.639 --> 00:04:49.349
Lastly, let me talk about Donald Trump's daily
press conferences.

00:04:49.349 --> 00:04:54.990
There is a growing debate over whether corporate
media should, should or shouldn't cover the

00:04:54.990 --> 00:04:59.539
daily coronavirus press conferences from Donald
Trump, because on the one hand.

00:04:59.539 --> 00:05:01.830
Donald Trump is using them to spread disinformation.

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:05.199
He's telling lies, he's cheerleading his handling
of Corona virus.

00:05:05.199 --> 00:05:09.749
On the other hand, it is the president speaking
about a national emergency and a pandemic.

00:05:09.749 --> 00:05:11.860
So what what should corporate media do?

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:15.550
So this is not to pat myself on the back because
lots of people are doing this.

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:22.020
What corporate media should do is to in real
time, fact check Donald Trump.

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:25.000
You've got to be ready when Trump says things
about testing.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:27.169
We've tested more people than anyone we say.

00:05:27.169 --> 00:05:29.840
We have three hundred and forty million people
on a per capita basis.

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:30.840
That's not true.

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:31.840
And that's what matters.

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:37.900
When Donald Trump says GM is making ventilators,
we point out and we say no, GM is making a

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:42.770
list of parts they would need and figuring
out where they would get the parts.

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:44.150
That's what GM has done so far.

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:46.250
GM is not making ventilators.

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:50.319
I don't know that corporate media is willing
to do it because they will take heat from

00:05:50.319 --> 00:05:52.110
the right if they do that.

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:57.740
That would be the responsible way to cover
Donald Trump's press conferences and publicly

00:05:57.740 --> 00:06:00.340
push for Trump not to be a part of them.

00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:04.240
Say we just want to hear from the doctors
and the public health experts.

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:05.240
That's what they should do.

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:05.247
I wouldn't expect them to do it.

